# thelooplocal

> Swift local snapshot of The Loop / Loopa. Sister of theloop.

## Purpose
Give a plain-language door to fitzyracing1/thelooplocal.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the local Loop files.
2. Use this clone to explain the idea.
3. Send the reader to theloop for the other Swift shelf.

## Key ideas
- The Loop, local copy
- Swift source
- Sister of theloop

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/thelooplocal
open_source()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to fitzyracing1/thelooplocal”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader wants the other Swift shelf → theloop

## What a person would notice
A named wrap on a local Loop door.

